From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: omarchy-dragon-sl7 <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 14:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] SL7 local: drm/msm/dpu: Compute the core clock per layer mixer

SL7 local: drm/msm/dpu: Compute the core clock per layer mixer

_dpu_core_perf_calc_clk() takes the pixel rate of the whole mode,
vtotal x hdisplay x vrefresh, as the floor of the core clock. When the
CRTC uses more than one layer mixer (3D merge, or one mixer per
interface) each mixer only handles its share of every line and the
mixers run in parallel, so the clock only has to sustain one mixer.
The mode filter already knows this: commit f5d079564c44 ("drm/msm/dpu:
Fix adjusted mode clock check for 3d merge") halves the adjusted mode
clock in dpu_crtc_mode_valid() when the SoC has 3D merge. The
performance calculation did not, so a mode accepted because of the
halving still voted the clock for the full width.

The plane side does not help either. dpu_plane_split() only splits a
plane in two pipes when it is wider than the SSPP line or when its clock
exceeds max_core_clk_rate, so a full-width plane is fetched by one pipe
that feeds both mixers, and that single pipe really needs the full-width
clock.

Make both sides per mixer:

 - Divide the mode clock by the number of mixers of the CRTC state.

 - Split a plane that is wider than one mixer of its stage into two
   pipes, as is done above max_core_clk_rate, so that each pipe needs no
   more than a mixer. The split is skipped when the pair cannot be
   fetched as two parallel rectangles (scaling, rotation, YUV, UBWC too
   wide, SSPP without smart DMA); such a plane keeps its single pipe and
   its full clock.

 - Take the plane clocks from the plane states being checked
   (drm_atomic_crtc_state_for_each_plane_state()) instead of the value
   cached in the committed plane state at atomic update. That value
   describes the previous commit, and was hidden by the full-width mode
   floor. With a per-mixer floor it would let one commit run on a clock
   computed without the new planes. The cached plane_clk member has no
   user left and is removed.

max_core_clk_rate, its debugfs file and the per-pipe limit check in
dpu_plane_atomic_check_pipe() are unchanged. With one mixer the mode
clock is divided by one and the extra split condition does not apply,
so the result is the same as before.

Numbers, Surface Laptop 7 13.8 inch (x1e80100, eDP 2304x1536 at 120 Hz,
vtotal 1579, two mixers with 3D merge, no DSC), clk_inefficiency_factor
105:

  before: 1579 x 2304 x 120 x 1.05 = 458.4 MHz -> 514 MHz OPP (MMCX NOM)
  after:  1579 x 1152 x 120 x 1.05 = 229.2 MHz -> 325 MHz OPP (MMCX SVS)

With max_core_clk_rate written to 325000000 through debugfs and a
modeset, the driver already splits the primary plane in two 1152 pixel
pipes and runs disp_cc_mdss_mdp_clk at 325 MHz, with no underrun in
dmesg; this patch reaches the same state without the cap, so external
modes up to the max_core_clk_rate limit stay available. External
displays: 4K at 120 Hz (about 537 MHz per mixer) and 5K at 60 Hz (about
476 MHz, from CVT-RB2 timings) stay valid and keep a sufficient clock
with two mixers; modes on one mixer are unchanged.

Risk: the per-mixer clock is only enough when no pipe is wider than a
mixer. A plane that cannot be split keeps its own full-width clock
through the plane term of the calculation, which now reads the checked
state, but a configuration that bypasses that term (a plane state whose
pipe_cfg is not final at check time) would run a full-width pipe on a
half clock and underrun. Platforms with several mixers per CRTC other
than the SL7 (dual DSI, DSC) take the same path and are untested.

Rationale: RUNTIME-PLAN.md power round 3, AWAKE-CX-MDP.md section 3.5
(MD-d). Expected on the SL7: mdp clock 325 MHz and MMCX SVS with the
screen on. Not built or measured yet.

Origin: ours
Upstream-Status: Not submitted (candidate: discuss with Dmitry Baryshkov and Jessica Zhang first)
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_core_perf.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_core_perf.c
@@ -88,26 +88,32 @@
  * @crtc: pointer to a crtc
  * @state: pointer to a crtc state
  * Return: returns max clk for all planes in crtc.
+ *
+ * The layer mixers of a CRTC work in parallel, each one on its own slice of
+ * every line, so the core clock has to sustain the pixel rate of one mixer,
+ * not of the whole mode. The plane clocks are taken from the plane states
+ * that are being checked, as the pipe configuration of those is final here,
+ * while the one stored in the committed state may describe other planes.
  */
 static u64 _dpu_core_perf_calc_clk(const struct dpu_perf_cfg *perf_cfg,
 		struct drm_crtc *crtc, struct drm_crtc_state *state)
 {
 	struct drm_plane *plane;
-	struct dpu_plane_state *pstate;
+	const struct drm_plane_state *plane_state;
 	struct drm_display_mode *mode;
 	u64 mode_clk;
+	u32 num_lm;
 
 	mode = &state->adjusted_mode;
 
 	mode_clk = (u64)mode->vtotal * mode->hdisplay * drm_mode_vrefresh(mode);
 
-	drm_atomic_crtc_for_each_plane(plane, crtc) {
-		pstate = to_dpu_plane_state(plane->state);
-		if (!pstate)
-			continue;
+	num_lm = max(dpu_crtc_get_num_lm(state), 1u);
+	mode_clk = div_u64(mode_clk, num_lm);
 
-		mode_clk = max(pstate->plane_clk, mode_clk);
-	}
+	drm_atomic_crtc_state_for_each_plane_state(plane, plane_state, state)
+		mode_clk = max(dpu_plane_state_calc_clk(plane_state, mode),
+			       mode_clk);
 
 	return dpu_core_perf_adjusted_mode_clk(mode_clk, perf_cfg);
 }
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_plane.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_plane.c
@@ -185,6 +185,34 @@
 }
 
 /**
+ * dpu_plane_state_calc_clk - calculate clock required by a plane state
+ * @state: Pointer to drm plane state
+ * @mode: Pointer to drm display mode
+ * Result: the highest clock needed by any pipe of the plane, 0 if the plane
+ * is not visible. It describes one pipe, as each pipe is fetched separately.
+ */
+u64 dpu_plane_state_calc_clk(const struct drm_plane_state *state,
+			     const struct drm_display_mode *mode)
+{
+	struct dpu_plane_state *pstate = to_dpu_plane_state(state);
+	u64 plane_clk = 0;
+	int i;
+
+	if (!state->visible)
+		return 0;
+
+	for (i = 0; i < PIPES_PER_PLANE; i++) {
+		if (!drm_rect_width(&pstate->pipe_cfg[i].src_rect))
+			continue;
+
+		plane_clk = max(plane_clk,
+				_dpu_plane_calc_clk(mode, &pstate->pipe_cfg[i]));
+	}
+
+	return plane_clk;
+}
+
+/**
  * _dpu_plane_calc_fill_level - calculate fill level of the given source format
  * @plane:		Pointer to drm plane
  * @pipe:		Pointer to software pipe
@@ -868,6 +896,39 @@
 	return 0;
 }
 
+static int dpu_plane_is_multirect_parallel_capable(struct dpu_hw_sspp *sspp,
+						   struct dpu_sw_pipe_cfg *pipe_cfg,
+						   const struct msm_format *fmt,
+						   uint32_t max_linewidth);
+
+/**
+ * dpu_plane_needs_mixer_split - check if a plane should be fetched per mixer
+ * @pipe_cfg: pipe configuration, clipped to the mixers of one stage
+ * @mode: display mode
+ * @sspp: SSPP used by the plane, NULL if not assigned yet
+ * @fmt: format of the plane
+ * @max_linewidth: maximum line width of an SSPP
+ * @mixer_width: width of one layer mixer
+ *
+ * The core clock is calculated for the pixel rate of one layer mixer. A plane
+ * fetched by a single pipe that is wider than a mixer needs more than that,
+ * so split it in two pipes, each of them feeding one mixer of the pair, when
+ * the hardware can do it.
+ */
+static bool dpu_plane_needs_mixer_split(struct dpu_sw_pipe_cfg *pipe_cfg,
+					const struct drm_display_mode *mode,
+					struct dpu_hw_sspp *sspp,
+					const struct msm_format *fmt,
+					uint32_t max_linewidth,
+					u32 mixer_width)
+{
+	u64 mixer_clk = (u64)mode->vtotal * mixer_width * drm_mode_vrefresh(mode);
+
+	return _dpu_plane_calc_clk(mode, pipe_cfg) > mixer_clk &&
+	       dpu_plane_is_multirect_parallel_capable(sspp, pipe_cfg, fmt,
+						       max_linewidth);
+}
+
 static int dpu_plane_split(struct drm_plane *plane,
 			   struct drm_plane_state *new_plane_state,
 			   const struct drm_crtc_state *crtc_state)
@@ -879,18 +940,22 @@
 	struct dpu_sw_pipe_cfg *pipe_cfg;
 	struct dpu_sw_pipe_cfg *r_pipe_cfg;
 	const struct drm_display_mode *mode = &crtc_state->adjusted_mode;
+	const struct msm_format *fmt = msm_framebuffer_format(new_plane_state->fb);
+	struct dpu_hw_sspp *sspp = NULL;
 	uint32_t max_linewidth;
-	u32 num_lm;
+	u32 num_lm, lms_in_stage, mixer_width;
 	int stage_id, num_stages;
 
 	max_linewidth = pdpu->catalog->caps->max_linewidth;
 
 	/* In non-virtual plane case, one mixer pair is always needed. */
 	num_lm = dpu_crtc_get_num_lm(crtc_state);
-	if (dpu_use_virtual_planes)
+	if (dpu_use_virtual_planes) {
 		num_stages = (num_lm + 1) / 2;
-	else
+	} else {
 		num_stages = 1;
+		sspp = dpu_rm_get_sspp(&kms->rm, pdpu->pipe);
+	}
 
 	/*
 	 * For wide plane that exceeds SSPP rectangle constrain, it needed to
@@ -948,9 +1013,18 @@
 		DPU_DEBUG_PLANE(pdpu, "Got clip src:" DRM_RECT_FMT " dst: " DRM_RECT_FMT "\n",
 				DRM_RECT_ARG(&pipe_cfg->src_rect), DRM_RECT_ARG(&pipe_cfg->dst_rect));
 
-		/* Split wide rect into 2 rect */
+		/*
+		 * Split wide rect into 2 rect, also when it is wider than one
+		 * of the mixers of this stage.
+		 */
+		lms_in_stage = min_t(u32, num_lm - stage_id * PIPES_PER_STAGE,
+				     PIPES_PER_STAGE);
+		mixer_width = drm_rect_width(&mixer_rect) / max(lms_in_stage, 1u);
 		if ((drm_rect_width(&pipe_cfg->src_rect) > max_linewidth) ||
-		     _dpu_plane_calc_clk(mode, pipe_cfg) > max_mdp_clk_rate) {
+		     _dpu_plane_calc_clk(mode, pipe_cfg) > max_mdp_clk_rate ||
+		     (lms_in_stage > 1 &&
+		      dpu_plane_needs_mixer_split(pipe_cfg, mode, sspp, fmt,
+						  max_linewidth, mixer_width))) {
 
 			if (drm_rect_width(&pipe_cfg->src_rect) > 2 * max_linewidth) {
 				DPU_DEBUG_PLANE(pdpu, "invalid src " DRM_RECT_FMT " line:%u\n",
@@ -1572,16 +1646,11 @@
 		pstate->needs_qos_remap = false;
 
 	pstate->plane_fetch_bw = 0;
-	pstate->plane_clk = 0;
 	for (i = 0; i < PIPES_PER_PLANE; i++) {
 		if (!drm_rect_width(&pstate->pipe_cfg[i].src_rect))
 			continue;
 		pstate->plane_fetch_bw += _dpu_plane_calc_bw(pdpu->catalog, fmt,
 							     &crtc->mode, &pstate->pipe_cfg[i]);
-
-		pstate->plane_clk = max(pstate->plane_clk,
-					_dpu_plane_calc_clk(&crtc->mode,
-							    &pstate->pipe_cfg[i]));
 	}
 }
 
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_plane.h
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_plane.h
@@ -25,7 +25,6 @@
  * @multirect_mode: parallel or time multiplex multirect mode
  * @pending:	whether the current update is still pending
  * @plane_fetch_bw: calculated BW per plane
- * @plane_clk: calculated clk per plane
  * @needs_dirtyfb: whether attached CRTC needs pixel data explicitly flushed
  * @layout:     framebuffer memory layout
  */
@@ -38,7 +37,6 @@
 	bool pending;
 
 	u64 plane_fetch_bw;
-	u64 plane_clk;
 
 	bool needs_dirtyfb;
 
@@ -50,6 +48,9 @@
 
 void dpu_plane_flush(struct drm_plane *plane);
 
+u64 dpu_plane_state_calc_clk(const struct drm_plane_state *state,
+			     const struct drm_display_mode *mode);
+
 void dpu_plane_set_error(struct drm_plane *plane, bool error);
 
 struct drm_plane *dpu_plane_init(struct drm_device *dev,
